WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.538
Hi! Plants can't walk or eat meals, so how do they stay alive? Today we'll look at a plant's leaves, stem and roots, and the job each part does.

2
00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:16.602
A plant has three main parts: the leaves, the stem and the roots.

3
00:00:16.752 --> 00:00:23.946
The leaves make food for the plant. They need sunlight to do this, so plants must be kept where there is light.

4
00:00:24.096 --> 00:00:34.626
The stem holds the plant up so the leaves can face the light. Tubes in the stem carry water and mineral salts up from the roots, and carry food from the leaves to other parts.

5
00:00:34.776 --> 00:00:44.946
The roots absorb water and mineral salts from the soil, and hold the plant firmly in the ground. Some roots also store food, like a carrot.

6
00:00:45.096 --> 00:00:50.586
How do we know the stem carries water? Put a balsam plant in red-coloured water.

7
00:00:50.736 --> 00:00:57.834
After a few hours, cut the stem across. You will see red dots: these are the tubes that carry water.

8
00:00:57.984 --> 00:01:07.242
The red water enters through the roots, travels up the stem and reaches the leaves. A plant with more leaves takes up more water.

9
00:01:07.392 --> 00:01:13.290
Watch out! Many pupils think a plant gets its food from the soil through its roots.

10
00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:20.394
In fact the roots take in water and mineral salts. The food is made by the leaves, using sunlight.

11
00:01:20.544 --> 00:01:28.002
Even the food in a carrot was made by the leaves, then carried down by the stem and stored in the root.

12
00:01:28.152 --> 00:01:37.650
Your turn! Which part of a plant absorbs water and mineral salts? Pause and think.

13
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:44.754
The roots. They also hold the plant firmly in the soil. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:58.458
Another one! A celery stalk is put in red water. Hours later, the cut stem shows red dots. What does this show? Pause and think.

15
00:01:58.608 --> 00:02:05.634
It shows that the stem has tubes that carry water up the plant. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:05.784 --> 00:02:16.002
Next one! The carrot we eat: which part of the plant is it, and what does it do? Pause and think.

17
00:02:16.152 --> 00:02:25.746
A carrot is a root. It absorbs water and mineral salts, and it stores the food made by the leaves. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:25.896 --> 00:02:36.330
Last one! A plant is kept in a dark cupboard for many days. What happens? Pause and think.

19
00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:44.538
Without sunlight, its leaves can't make food, so the plant grows weaker and weaker. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:44.688 --> 00:02:57.546
Remember: leaves make food for the plant using sunlight. The stem holds the plant up and carries water, mineral salts and food. The roots absorb water and mineral salts and hold the plant in the soil.

21
00:02:57.696 --> 00:03:03.138
Look at a plant at home and find its leaves, stem and roots!

